# The x64 board's packages: its kernel and the rendered layout files for the
# QEMU/UEFI target.
#
# Two entries and not one, because they are two decisions. mos-board-x64 is the
# layout -- /etc/fstab, the ESP mount unit, the RAUC grub configuration -- and
# moves when boards/x64/board.env does. mos-kernel-x64 is the kernel this
# repository builds from boards/x64/bsp, and moves when its pin or its config
# does. It replaced Debian's linux-image-amd64, which arrived as a Depends and
# brought an initramfs with it (PLAN-074).
#
# NAMED HERE ALTHOUGH mos-board-x64 ALREADY DEPENDS ON IT. A package reachable
# only through another package's Depends is one no resolution names, so it
# never appears in _out/<board>/rootfs-packages.txt and
# tests/rootfs-manifest-test.sh reports it unreachable -- which is the right
# answer for a package nothing selects and the wrong one for the kernel.
mos-board-x64
mos-kernel-x64
